{
  "id": "introduction-introduction",
  "slug": "introduction",
  "title": "Introduction",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "overview-characteristics",
      "heading": "Overview & Characteristics",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Batch applications are programs designed to process large volumes of data automatically without human intervention. They are commonly used when a business needs offline, scheduled, or bulk data processing."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 29,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "what-are-batch-applications",
      "heading": "What Are Batch Applications?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Batch applications execute tasks in bulk, usually at scheduled times, and without manual input."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 14,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "typical-examples",
          "heading": "Typical Examples",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Generating monthly financial statements",
                "Producing business reports (daily/weekly/monthly)",
                "Running statistical calculations (e.g., sales trends)",
                "Indexing files and documents for search",
                "Sending scheduled communications (e.g., monthly invoices)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 26,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "why-batch-applications-are-useful",
          "heading": "Why Batch Applications Are Useful",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "They handle heavy workloads efficiently.",
                "They avoid impacting peak-hour performance.",
                "They can run at night or during low-traffic periods."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 19,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "data-exchange-between-systems",
      "heading": "Data Exchange Between Systems",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Batch processes are widely used to share data between two systems when real-time synchronization isn't necessary."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 16,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "common-usage-scenario",
          "heading": "Common Usage Scenario",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "One system exports data (e.g., user updates, inventory changes) into files, which are then imported into another system as a batch job during non-peak hours."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 25,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "reasons-to-use-batch-data-exchange",
          "heading": "Reasons to Use Batch Data Exchange",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Data Security: Direct access to the data of one system might not be allowed or desirable. Exporting controlled files is safer.",
                "Incompatible APIs or Formats: When systems don’t share compatible APIs, protocols, or data structures.",
                "Business Does Not Require Real-Time Data: Some processes tolerate delay (e.g., inventory sync once a day)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 51,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "example",
          "heading": "Example",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Online Store → Warehouse System"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Online Store System",
                "Batch Application",
                "Warehouse System"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Generates daily inventory update (CSV)",
                  "Reads, processes, validates data",
                  "Updates stock levels in warehouse DB"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "This avoids direct integration and reduces load during peak hours."
            },
            {
